Z||000002||Uaana||08-27-2001||01:01 AM||||Anyone else have some input on this gremlin?<BR>I have a similar problem. 3-4 just fine. But first and second I have to force into. almost feels like something is "bound up?"<BR>Linkage and bracket from the firewall to the tranni look ok. <BR>Is it possible for the cables to get messed up under the console?<BR>Or am I looking at a new/rebuild of the tranni for bad syncros?<BR>And yes the clutch is brand new.||||reg||1
Z||000003||V8Dreamer||08-27-2001||02:14 PM||||I had the same prob in my isuzu 5spd....it turned out to be a piece of the plastic speedo gear I accidentally fed the tranny for breakfast a couple of mos earlier(doh!).  For me the fix was to remove the shifting mechanism and voila, there was a nice piece of purple plastic sittin under there blocking movement to 1st and 2nd gear.......now, you probably won't find any purple plastic, but I'd disconnect the shift cables and try to shift it manually, if you still can't budge em, remove the assembly and check for obvious debris.  This saved me a day of dropping the cradle and swapping trannies.....so I'd say before you go ripping everything apart, check it out.<P>Ryan||||reg||1
